On Dec 2, 3:35 am, Sledgen <rs_sle...@hotmail.com> wrote:
> Given you have another WoW waiting for you at the castle you can
> definately afford whatever you need armourwise. A magic marker is
> definately a good idea. For armour, speed boots and a cloak of
> displacement are worthwhile. Gauntlets of power are good for people of
> low experience but gauntlets of dexterity will do just as good.
> Enchant them all very highly, will help you get through the learning
> curve in Gehennom. Don't worry about a magical helm, they arnt worth
> wishes and a elven helm can be enchanted really high.

It depends.  With a robe and a sufficiently enchanted helm of
brilliance, even a Valk can be a moderatly proficient spell
caster.  Being able to cast cure sickness at 0% failure has
saved me once or twice as a Valk; cone of cold or the fire spell
make useful alternatives to daggers, e.g. on watery levels where
you would loose them otherwise.

Unless you're going to try throwing Mojo (I don't), I wouldn't
worry about the guantlets.  Gauntlets of dexterity don't make
that much difference compared to plain leather gloves.  (On the
other hand, with the number of wishes he's going to have...)

Another thing to consider might be blessed scrolls of genocide
(although I find I'm using genocide less and less).

With three artifacts already in the game, I probably wouldn't
risk wishing for one, but if I did, it would definitly be
Magicbane.  Dual weaponing Magicbane and a silver saber isn't as
powerful as using Grayswandir, but it's generally enough, and
unless the bad liches have been genocided, you definitly want to
wield Magicbane if possible.  (On the other hand, my first
ascension was a Valk with Grayswandir and a katana.  Both at +7.
With speed, you can normally arrange things to get two swipes in
before the monster starts hitting, and with that combination,
two swipes is enough for just about anything.)

> Other then that, save most of the wishes in your castle wand for
> later. You never know when you will really need them.

And often, for things you wouldn't have considered earlier.  On
my last ascension, I had to visit all three altars, and ran out
of teleport wands.  I ended up spending about three wishes on
those (and probably wouldn't have ascended without those
wishes).

